# ISO-X 0.4.0 — Debian Trixie amd64 desktop and hardware coverage
# Debian Trixie uses split firmware packages rather than Ubuntu's aggregate `linux-firmware` package.
# `firmware-linux` and vendor packages below are its Debian package equivalents.
# `firmware-ralink` is virtual/provided by firmware-misc-nonfree; no standalone install line is required.
# `firmware-mediatek` and firmware-nvidia-graphics may require Trixie backports;
# this stable-only image avoids mixing suites; firmware-misc-nonfree ships the stable Trixie firmware set.
